# Vespa nearestNeighbor — dense retrieval by hand
#
# rank-profile `dense` (chunk.sd) takes one input: query(q), a tensor<float>(x[4096]).
# You cannot type 4096 floats, so generate the body first:
#
#   uv run python tools/gen_vespa_query.py "engine oil servicing" --package package-a
#
# That writes var/http/dense-search.json (git-ignored), which the first block
# below sends verbatim. Re-run the generator to change the query, then re-send.
#
# Scores: rank-profile `dense` is closeness(field, embedding). Vectors are
# L2-normalized by the provider, so distance-metric prenormalized-angular means
# cosine == inner product; relevance is in (0, 1], 1.0 = identical direction.

@query = http://localhost:8080

### Dense search — body generated by tools/gen_vespa_query.py
POST {{query}}/search/
Content-Type: application/json

< ../../var/http/dense-search.json

### Shape of the payload the generator writes — for reference, DO NOT send
# (the vector is truncated; sending this errors with a tensor dimension mismatch)
# POST {{query}}/search/
# {
#   "yql": "select * from chunk where ({targetHits:10, approximate:false}nearestNeighbor(embedding, q)) and package contains \"package-a\"",
#   "ranking.profile": "dense",
#   "input.query(q)": { "values": [0.0123, -0.0456, "... 4094 more floats ..."] },
#   "hits": 10
# }

### Verify a document really carries a 4096-dim vector (id from 01-documents.http)
# The embedding field has no `summary` in the schema, so search never returns it;
# document/v1 does.
GET {{query}}/document/v1/learnarken/chunk/docid/c4775a03c5de0039
